{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming","id":93985,"title":"Cursed Necropolis: DC spoilers are coming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-18T18:23:48-07:00","id":93985,"title":"Cursed Necropolis: DC spoilers are coming","content":"Book is now in layout. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MummyTheCurse\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://facebook.com/security/hsts-pixel.gif?c=3.2.5\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MummyTheCurse\" target=\"_blank\"> Log in or sign up to view </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MummyTheCurse\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/MummyTheCurse </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> See posts, photos and more on Facebook. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T19:04:31-07:00","id":94010,"title":"","content":"Well, that's unexpected honestly. So what took the old editor 7 months took this new one...a few weeks. That's not fair, they probably only needed to finish up stuff from the old editor. STILL! Very unexpected. I'm waiting for the DC preview with vim and vigor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T21:48:26-07:00","id":94090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RisTigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=94010#post94010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's unexpected honestly. So what took the old editor 7 months took this new one...a few weeks. That's not fair, they probably only needed to finish up stuff from the old editor. STILL! Very unexpected. I'm waiting for the DC preview with vim and vigor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't take seven months. DC went to editing in February.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T23:36:45-07:00","id":94141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=94090#post94090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't take seven months. DC went to editing in February.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry! Got that number from the update thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:35:41-07:00","id":94300,"title":"","content":"Muhahahaha! Hell yes! This is a god (judge?) send for a guy who's in the beginning stages of a D.C.-based chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T10:32:57-07:00","id":94326,"title":"","content":"DC is one I'm really looking forward to, it should be an excellent chance for CAS to show us how he pictures Mummy society working, what kinds of things he expects characters to get up to, etc.<br /> <br /> Because the Pre-made characters seem to be from a different game tonally entirely...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T13:34:01-07:00","id":94426,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really feel an example city in the core would've done Mummy well. I wonder where we'd all be if the Kickstarter never got the DC Citybook stretch goal. I predict it'll be like a 'second half' to what <i>Guildhalls</i> provided","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T19:18:27-07:00","id":94618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=94426#post94426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I really feel an example city in the core would've done Mummy well. I wonder where we'd all be if the Kickstarter never got the DC Citybook stretch goal. I predict it'll be like a 'second half' to what <i>Guildhalls</i> provided</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it kinda did with Rio and the mini adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T20:21:36-07:00","id":94662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=94090#post94090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't take seven months. DC went to editing in February.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to backlogged Monday Meeting notes it was first as being in editing from the 31st of January. Making the total time spent in editing 7 weeks. Five of those seven were with the old editor. Though <br /> <br /> Doing some digging...<br /> <br /> Seems (from the Monday Morning blogs) that DC went into writing in July last year (interestingly the books cover was approved at this time, art usually comes later right?). First draft entered redlining in September. Redlining then lasted until mid-October when second drafts started being revised by the writers. Mid-December was when it got handed back for a developer-pass (which I presume is another round of red-lining). It entered editing at the end of January and has staid there until now. <br /> <br /> Considering the book is, according to the information handed out to Kickstarter backers, 80 pages long some of these stretches could be seen as a little stretched. I've never redlined anything, but its anything like formatting, proofing and correcting academic papers then 6 weeks for 80 pages seems a little extreme. Obviously their were problems with the editor, as demonstrated by the fact the new one managed to get it done in 2 weeks were the last one was on 5 before handing off. <br /> <br /> I'm grateful that we get a book that actually explains how modern Mummy society functions and how the Guilds practical interact in a local sense in the modern day. It was something sorely missing from the Core that Guildhalls did not do a great deal to fix (to be fair it was never that books job to do so, and it did flesh out the Guilds well). I mirror Reseru on this point. <br /> <br /> \u200bI maintain the my skeptical stance on the Mummy lines schedule. I have faith that DC will be good because the writers worked on one of my favorite Masquerade books and the products obviously been gone over with a fine tooth comb for quality. However, I'm saying we don't see the first draft pdf until the end of April at earliest. There is still all the art to sort-out and then approvals and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T21:53:26-07:00","id":94708,"title":"","content":"Mm, yes, you're correct. My notes say it was the last week of January rather than the first week of February, as I had remembered. But that's seven weeks, not seven months. The editing process is four to six weeks for anything smaller than a 20th anniversary edition. Exact deadlines depend on editor workloads -- like with any other part of the process, we're usually working around day jobs.<br /> <br /> In this case, the original editor hit a problem and flipped the book back to Colin, who reallocated the work. We lost a few weeks, but it's moved to art direction now. (The cover was done way early because we were commissioning a lot of work from that artist at the same time.)<br /> <br /> Redlining's also different from correcting an academic paper, but the development process is a fairly long thing to explain. Maybe I should do a dev blog describing it from beginning to end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T22:35:54-07:00","id":94719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm grateful that we get a book that actually explains how modern Mummy society functions and how the Guilds practical interact in a local sense in the modern day. It was something sorely missing from the Core that Guildhalls did not do a great deal to fix (to be fair it was never that books job to do so, and it did flesh out the Guilds well). I mirror Reseru on this point. </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize this was what DC was for. So the core was basically made for solo or group mummy stores. Guildhalls was for a more political and global game of the arisen. So if DC is for a local mummy society in DC, I'm wondering if it will flesh out how the World of Darkness as a whole reacts to mummies? That was something that was sorely missing in the core as well. I think the only one we got any info on was vampires? Can anyone confirm or deny that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T05:00:27-07:00","id":94855,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't necessarily say that each book lines up to a different scale of <i>Mummy</i> play.<br /> <br /> And, to Eldagusto, I don't really see how it did. A mini-adventure's setting location isn't a substitution for an appendix city write-up as is standard in other core books. Nor did the adventure detail how Arisen nomes function (nor should it have done so, at that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T05:09:11-07:00","id":94860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=94708#post94708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redlining's also different from correcting an academic paper, but the development process is a fairly long thing to explain. Maybe I should do a dev blog describing it from beginning to end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think that sort of thing would be a good idea in general. I think a lot of the complaints about development times come from people having an idea of how long the process should take, given their own experience with creating media or similar projects (I've been using Master Degree's for example). So if you explain exactly what goes on in each part and how long those things take on average then people can adjust their mental image of how long some things should take. <br /> <br /> The other issue is that certain projects and lines seem to be much, much quicker through this process (without any comparative drop in quality) then others. For Example:<br /> <br /> Mummy's been out a year in POD basically and 14 months for the Kickstarter backers. It's had a single splat book (Guildhalls) and a couple of Kickstater extra's (Wallpapers, Ready Made Characters, Character Sheets) released in that time. <br /> <br /> Demon's been out to Kickstater backers for about 2 Months. I think the POD's out either end of March or beginning of April. However, it seems that in the next 14 months that its going to get a lot more line development e.g. Players Guide, Heirs to Hell, Demon Seeds, Ready Made Characters, Splintered City: Seattle, Storytellers Guide, Translation Guide, Demon Story Interface. Honestly I can see the majority of these delivered to backers and players in the next 12 months. Considering the majority are already in the redline stage or further at current. <br /> <br /> I think shedding light on the development issue may waylay some peoples thoughts on this issue a bit. Because without any transparency it seems that one of two situations are occurring: <br /> <br /> 1) That Onyx Path is supporting certain lines over others. I don't truly believe this, though it is fair to say that White Wolf in the past has tried to give people what they want and some games are just more popular then others e.g. the extra books in Changelings release cycle, the fact that their are more Vampire and Mage books then Werewolf ones. <br /> <br /> 2) That one Dev Team/Line Developer is far more hard working/passionate/on the ball when it comes to getting the line he/she is shepherding out then the other one. Which is not a nice impression to give in general I think. <br /> <br /> Obviously then there are the people that realize that maybe the writers on one line just have had better luck and had more time to develop their game and the comparative speeds are nothing that either group has any really control over. <br /> <br /> P.s. RisTigger I would not count on that. I think how Mummy's interact with other supernaturals won't be covered till the final book in the line Sothis Ascendent. As far as I know it MIGHT be in the writing stage at current, but I think its schedules for the last 3 months or so of 2014 so...yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T18:44:13-07:00","id":95324,"title":"","content":"I'll add an explanation of the process to my list of dev blogs. Ethan Skemp wrote a fantastic walkthrough back when we were at White Wolf, and many parts of the process are the same as in those days. Unfortunately, I don't have a copy anymore.<br /> <br /> As for how long it takes... truth is, deadlines for each step of an individual project are often set based on the team involved. For example, if I know I can get every member of a team on a book immediately, it might take only two thirds as long as a book where one or more writers has another contract to attend to. In a few cases, I've rescheduled books so that I can work with a writer I specifically need. Another example: the difference between a four week and six week editing job is often the editor's workload rather than the length of the book.<br /> <br /> Add to that schedule slippage. We have only two or three writers or developers who aren't juggling a day job, and most of them have families, too. I'm one of relatively RPG workers I know who's both full time and has no kids. We <i>have</i> been tightening up the schedule and improving our planning -- that's one reason <i>Demon</i> is moving along well. It's still got slips, though -- <i>Vampire</i>, Kickstarters, and <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i> all pushed back the <i>Translation Guide</i>. Even within that, we lose time when somebody's child is sick, or development gets pushed back because another book needs attention, and so on. We don't ruthlessly drop contributors as soon as they ask for an extension -- there were times at other jobs when I've had to do that and I don't like it. All of that goes for artists as well as authors.<br /> <br /> We do our best to be transparent about our workflow. It's easiest and most honest for us to talk about what's going on with a book at this moment (the Monday Meeting update) than anything else. We show our initial target dates and we try to keep up a flow of communication about where each book is between first draft and publication. Explaining in more detail what each of those steps mean is a good idea, though.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, we haven't moved any resources from <i>Mummy</i> to other lines. The only place <i>Mummy</i> books bump up against other books is in the art queue, and so far I don't think <i>Mummy</i> books have waited any longer for art direction and layout than anything else. (I'd have to double check that with Mike; he schedules and manages all of that after my people have handed off the book.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T19:07:33-07:00","id":95336,"title":"","content":"Is there a chance Ethan has a copy of those livejournals? I remember those and really wish I had set someone to record them over the course of my mission-those were valuable discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T05:55:21-07:00","id":95543,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Rose, for your input. I'm grateful for any writer or developer stopping by the Mummy forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:10:11-07:00","id":95649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=95336#post95336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a chance Ethan has a copy of those livejournals? I remember those and really wish I had set someone to record them over the course of my mission-those were valuable discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were really good. They're all still up, it's just impossible to find anything. That's one of the reasons I try to tag all my dev blogs responsibly these days. If you read Ethan's post back then, you know the basic steps. Where we've changed is in adapting the specifics to an entirely remote work environment. We've also started frontloading design more than we did in the old days -- for a lot of books, I get my writers working together before I've done the final outline.<br /> <br /> reseru, I'm glad to stop in. Since <i>Mummy</i> is CAS's baby, I don't usually have a lot to contribute. But being the producer, I can always talk about production!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T10:08:51-07:00","id":95732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=95324#post95324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Add to that schedule slippage. We have only two or three writers or developers who aren't juggling a day job, and most of them have families, too. I'm one of relatively RPG workers I know who's both full time and has no kids. <b>We <i>have</i> been tightening up the schedule and improving our planning -- that's one reason <i>Demon</i> is moving along well. It's still got slips, though -- <i>Vampire</i>, Kickstarters, and <i>The Demon Seed Collection</i> all pushed back the <i>Translation Guide</i>.</b> Even within that, we lose time when somebody's child is sick, or development gets pushed back because another book needs attention, and so on. We don't ruthlessly drop contributors as soon as they ask for an extension -- there were times at other jobs when I've had to do that and I don't like it. All of that goes for artists as well as authors.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, we haven't moved any resources from <i>Mummy</i> to other lines. The only place <i>Mummy</i> books bump up against other books is in the art queue, and so far I don't think <i>Mummy</i> books have waited any longer for art direction and layout than anything else. (I'd have to double check that with Mike; he schedules and manages all of that after my people have handed off the book.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've highlighted because I feel that point is an important one. Mummy was my first experience with the Onyx Path production model. As such I kinda just presumed that the pace which its development was pretty much the norm. Same with the style of the development. <br /> <br /> Demon kinda changed all that for me. I backed Demon and you guys have been pretty amazing ever since with it: -<br /> - Regular updates on the Monday Meeting blog, <br /> - Separate articles about Demon in general on the website.<br /> - Lots of interaction with the fans of the forums (and not only the Demon forum)<br /> - Just now at the 2/3 month mark when all communication dropped off with Mummy you guys did an special update e-mail for Kickstarter backers explain each project's development.<br /> - Then you did a special post about the next non-Kickstarter Demon book. <br /> <br /> The level of attention to the community and transparency from Demon as a project has frankly, been amazing. I can google the writers for any upcoming Demon book if I wanted to. Its not something I'd normally do in the process of a books development, but the point is you guys have given that much info that I could if I felt like it. <br /> <br /> Yes as you say Rose the Translation Guide got bumped. However, that's one slippage that relatively small and the product in question is not vital to playing the game nor does it add a new dynamic to the game. Its a toolkit for backwards compatibility with Fallen. <br /> <br /> With all the above recently opening my eyes to what a line can be in both its well organised production and its level of community forethought and saturation I look at the same things in Mummy and I'm just disappointed frankly. Which makes me frustrated, because I love this game and I really feel it gets at some important ideas within its context. I feel like I'm in a niche crowd by even following/buying/supporting Mummy (because lets face it its about as niche as Promethean really) and as such within this smaller niche community their should be a dialogue between the fans and the creators. Much like their is in the more widely liked Demon. <br /> <br /> I've already mentioned release pace between lines as an example. Another is community involvement. Rose, by simply being on this thread and posting a few times about the production method has been more involved and transparent about the creative part of the game then CAS has been since the game was released. Likewise, the last time Kickstarter backers got any update or news about further Kickstarter related products for Mummy was in September 2013, six months ago. There have been no article posts outside the Monday Meeting blog about Mummy since the teaser for Guildhalls in July (except to announce things like the pdf of the Ready Made characters and ST Screen for general sale). Demon's suffered minor slippage on one project, every single Mummy product has been delayed by at least a month and these delays are only growing bigger and bigger as the line goes on. <br /> <br /> This is only compounded by the fact that a lot of these upcoming products add whole new aspects to the game. Guildhalls allows for actual guild politics to be a thing on a global or regional scale. Good luck running Deceived plot with the resources we currently have for them. Or doing city based Mummy politics and Guild Structure without DC. <br /> <br /> The truly sad thing is that all the above things I've listed could be resolved or at least explained with a couple of forum posts an e-mail and a general news article on the Onyx Path site. It does not take a lot of effort to do that sort of thing, it might take a few hours to write such things. It would go a very, very long way with a community that (judging by the activity on this forum at least) is growing increasingly detached.<br /> <br /> \u200bOK, that's my vent out of the way. Rose, if you can poke Colin and get him to talk to us in same fashion that would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T06:17:35-07:00","id":96306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=95649#post95649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">reseru, I'm glad to stop in. Since <i>Mummy</i> is CAS's baby, I don't usually have a lot to contribute. But being the producer, I can always talk about production</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I know you aren't involved with Mummy but it's good that someone is on here that's developed or written for Onyx Path!<br /> <br /> Hawthorn brought up some good points (especially how essential the supplements are to run different aspects of the game), and I don't want this thread to turn into what the <i>2014 Mummy Previews &amp; Releases</i> thread was/is, but I do want to say this one bit: more than anything else, I think all of our concerns aren't necessarily that the books have been delayed but rather that there's so little communication about them.<br /> <br /> CAS is a judge for the...Ennies? Or something, so he has a lot of RPG books to get through at the moment, and everyone pretty much has a day job, too. So, I understand books being delayed. But what makes us feel like the line has already been forsaken is that there's so little word about what's going on. <i>Book of the Deceived</i> was estimated to be <b>released</b> in Novemeber, and five months later (before we were finally told a writer dropped) all we knew was that it was being <b>redlined</b>. When we ask, &quot;What's going on?&quot; it's not, &quot;I'm so angry why is this delayed how could they!&quot; It's, &quot;What happened, because I'm curious about a game I'm interested in and redlining for five months after estimated release seems odd.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>The Fallen World Chronicles</i> isn't even on an OP schedule (though we know it's shooting for November), and I know more about it than a book that was estimated to be released five months ago! Between this forum and the old one there's been half a dozen threads about people wondering how to implement the Deceived into their Mummy game, and the best answer anyone has it, &quot;Wait for <i>Book of the Deceived</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> So <b>anyone</b> showing up, Rose, is a good sign <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Plus. you didn't capitalize my username so I love you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T12:11:22-07:00","id":96474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/93985-cursed-necropolis-dc-spoilers-are-coming?p=96306#post96306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, I know you aren't involved with Mummy but it's good that someone is on here that's developed or written for Onyx Path!<br /> <br /> Hawthorn brought up some good points (especially how essential the supplements are to run different aspects of the game), and I don't want this thread to turn into what the <i>2014 Mummy Previews &amp; Releases</i> thread was/is, but I do want to say this one bit: more than anything else, I think all of our concerns aren't necessarily that the books have been delayed but rather that there's so little communication about them.<br /> <br /> CAS is a judge for the...Ennies? Or something, so he has a lot of RPG books to get through at the moment, and everyone pretty much has a day job, too. So, I understand books being delayed. But what makes us feel like the line has already been forsaken is that there's so little word about what's going on. <i>Book of the Deceived</i> was estimated to be <b>released</b> in Novemeber, and five months later (before we were finally told a writer dropped) all we knew was that it was being <b>redlined</b>. When we ask, &quot;What's going on?&quot; it's not, &quot;I'm so angry why is this delayed how could they!&quot; It's, &quot;What happened, because I'm curious about a game I'm interested in and redlining for five months after estimated release seems odd.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>The Fallen World Chronicles</i> isn't even on an OP schedule (though we know it's shooting for November), and I know more about it than a book that was estimated to be released five months ago! Between this forum and the old one there's been half a dozen threads about people wondering how to implement the Deceived into their Mummy game, and the best answer anyone has it, &quot;Wait for <i>Book of the Deceived</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> So <b>anyone</b> showing up, Rose, is a good sign <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Plus. you didn't capitalize my username so I love you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, just all of this. It illustrates the point I've been trying to make in two threads now far better then I have currently managed. I like Reseru don't want this to turn into a second 2014 Mummy Previews and Release thread so I am going to leave this topic alone after this post. I just wanted to show some solidarity with Reseru and the points we as fans are trying to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}